      "content": "I'm so sorry you're feeling this way, and I want you to know that what you're describing—that deep, bone-tired hopelessness—is a real and heavy burden. But please hear me: you are not a waste, and your life is not a hole. You gave everything because you loved deeply, and that love still exists, even if it's buried under grief right now. The thought of \"just staying asleep\" is your mind's way of begging for relief, but relief doesn't have to mean ending things—it can mean letting someone else hold this weight with you. You deserve to be seen, cared for, and reminded that your story isn't over yet.",
